    {
      "id": "82d5c36e-ce50-450e-950b-ef2cdb0f8d6e",
      "name": "Sticky Note7",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -2480,
        -272
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 572,
        "height": 1248,
        "content": "## Auto Post to YouTube Shorts / YouTube.\n### This n8n template demonstrates how to use Gdrive , Airtable and YouTube API to auto post videos to Youtube.\n\nAuto Uploading can be done the same way to Youtube or Youtube shorts.\n\n## How it works\n* At a random time throughout the day we wil start the flow - using the schedule trigger and random minutes and wait nodes.\n* We'll import our required video via our Google Drive folder.\n* The we are going to check it's file size and if it too large we will compress the file size using Cloudinary.\n* We will then use AI to write Hashtags and a short caption.\n* Then we update our Airtable records - we will use Airtable to keep track of what we are uploading!\n* Upload the video to YouTube\n* Delete it from the Gdrive so we don't upload the same video again\n\n## How to use\n*The shedule trigger is set with CRON expression to run in specific days and hours , you can modify it as you want.\n*In case you don't know what CRON is - https://crontab.guru/#0_19_*_*\n\n## Requirements\n* YouTube API\n* Google drive API\n* Gemini API\n* Airtable Set-UP\n* Telegram chat bot API (optional)\n* Google Cloud Console Storage\n* Cloudinary\n\n## Need Help?\n\nask in the [Forum](https://community.n8n.io/)!\n\n"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "0cded8c3-7738-4009-a143-6f4ed366cf09",
      "name": "random minutes",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "position": [
        -1312,
        208
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "const randomMinutes = Math. floor (Math. random() * 840) + 1;\nconst delayMs = randomMinutes * 60 * 1000;\n\nreturn [\n{\njson: {\ndelay: delayMs,\nminutes: randomMinutes\n}\n}\n  ];"
      },
      "typeVersion": 2
    },
